# Yersinia pestis, the hierarchical 14+12 VNTR scheme of Li et al. 2013 (PLoS ONE 8:e66567).
# The first fourteen loci are the first typing step, which places an isolate in a major
# population; the last twelve are the second step, which resolves it to a sub-population. They are
# kept in that order, so the first fourteen digits of a profile are the first step result.
#
# Primers and reference values are Table S2 of the paper, which gives both for all 88 loci it
# surveyed and encodes the reference values in the locus name as NAME_<unit>bp_<size>bp_<n>U,
# measured in CO92. Nine of the twenty-six loci were first described in that paper; the rest carry
# the names of Pourcel et al. (yp...ms...) and Klevytska et al. (M...), whose primers this paper
# reuses. Those are not always the primers the bundled Pourcel panel uses for the same locus, so
# the products differ in size; see scheme.yml.
#
# The search window is derived, not published: it runs from the length of the amplicon with no
# repeat to that length plus twenty-five repeats beyond the reference.

